From 0869ea09291a42e7a44dcede4ab7d0d77efa69d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atomchild411 <143453386+atomchild411@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 13:19:58 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Content extensions: no misaligned loads or stores

Strict-alignment CPUs (MIPS) fault where x86 and ARM do not:
- SerializedNFA wrote its arrays back to back, so the uint64_t actions could
  start 4 bytes off 8 in the mapped file: each array now starts at a
  multiple of its element's alignment (compiling a rule list crashed with a
  bus error in NFAToDFA).
- DFA bytecode, serialized actions and strings are packed byte by byte:
  multi-byte values are now copied in and out rather than read and written
  through casts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
